    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a purely derived, read-only field \u2014 formatted from two values already present on the `Owner` at creation (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`). This makes it directly analogous to the existing `displayName` and `initials` fields, which are computed in the MapStruct mapper rather than stored, so I followed that same pattern rather than adding a stored column or a new OfficeFloor function.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   This produces e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`, where `26` is the last two digits of the registration-date year (zero-padded, so years like 2007 \u2192 `07`).\n\nSince it's derived from the owner's own returned fields, it's serialized on both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses with no persistence changes. The `coreMembershipNumberFormat` acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
